# Where the API gateway lives.
#
# Auth, API keys, quota and billing all live in the new-api gateway, which has
# its own hostname so its console works: the console is a single-page app that
# hardcodes its asset and API paths at the root, so a path prefix on this origin
# cannot serve it.
#
# This is the only gateway setting the app reads. There is no NEXT_PUBLIC_*
# variable: the browser never talks to the gateway directly, so nothing about it
# needs to be inlined into the client bundle.
#
# Server-side only. On the VM this points at the gateway container directly:
# Caddy routes by Host header, and a server-side call carries the service name as
# its host, so going through Caddy would fall through to the site and answer HTML.
BACKEND_API_URL="http://new-api:3000"

# Signs the session cookie this app issues.
#
# The gateway's own cookies cannot be used: they are SameSite=Strict, host-only
# for the gateway, and do not authenticate its management API at all. Its access
# token lives 15 minutes and is renewed with a refresh token, so both are held
# server-side in this cookie. Changing this value signs everyone out.
#
# Generate with: openssl rand -hex 32
SESSION_SECRET=""
